# Initial Setup's DroneCAN/UAVCAN page, ported from GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigDroneCAN.cs
# over crates/mp-dronecan (ExtLibs/DroneCAN).
#
# The claim: Activate binds the interface list again - SLCAN chosen, the network list hidden
# (ConfigDroneCAN.cs:39-57, 1685-1700); Connect on MAVLinkCAN1 empties the node grid, disables the
# lists, says "Disconnect", enables Filter and starts StartMavlinkCAN - MAV_CMD_CAN_FORWARD for bus 1
# a second later and every second after, the vehicle's CAN_FRAMEs to our node 127 and its frames
# back as CAN_FRAMEs on bus 0 (:85-196, 1637-1683). Our node's own NodeStatus is heard by itself
# (InvokeMessageReceived), so node 127 is a row: "?" with the status's numbers, then OK and
# OPERATIONAL, then - its GetNodeInfo answered by itself - "org.missionplanner" (:293-460;
# DroneCAN.cs:300-386). The Menu cell opens the node's menu; Parameters asks node 127 for its
# parameters behind "Getting Params", which our node does not answer, so after two seconds the
# parameter window opens empty (:657-671; DroneCAN.cs:534-602). Filter's window lists all 155
# message types and its "ALL" box sends CAN_FILTER_MODIFY once the forwarding loop runs
# (:782-866). Stats opens its window (:1394-1478). Inspector, not ported, says so on the status
# line. Disconnect, and leaving the page, stop the bus (:673-709).
#
# What it cannot check: SITL has no DroneCAN node of its own on a CAN bus it forwards (CAN_FORWARD
# goes unanswered or refused, and no CAN_FRAME comes back), so the grid holds only node 127 -
# nodes heard from the bus, their info and parameters, firmware updates and the passthroughs are
# the unit tests' (config::dronecan, mp-dronecan's jobs and node tests). SLCAN would take this
# script's own MAVLink port, and the multicast buses need a SITL started with a multicast CAN bus;
# neither is driven here.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm. Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-dronecan.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen params
window 1600x1200
budget 25
# A first budget, set by hand until a passing run records one.
# A config.xml of its own, so the "Show me again?" boxes this script clicks are not already
# suppressed by the settings of the machine running it.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
env MP_LOG_DIR $WORK
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
# The vehicle first: a click before its first heartbeat is a click the screen may forget
# (vehicle.connected only says the link is open).
expect vehicle.count > 0
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

click tab-setup
expect config.dronecan.active false
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
click setup-page-ConfigDroneCAN
expect setup.page ConfigDroneCAN
expect config.dronecan.active true
expect config.dronecan.interface SLCAN
expect config.dronecan.network.visible false
expect config.dronecan.button Connect
expect config.dronecan.connected false
expect config.dronecan.lists.enabled true
expect config.dronecan.exitslcan true
expect config.dronecan.log false
expect config.dronecan.bus none
expect config.dronecan.window none

# The interface list: MAVLinkCAN1.
click dronecan-interface
click dronecan-interface-list-1
expect config.dronecan.interface MAVLinkCAN1
expect config.dronecan.network.visible false

# Connect: the forwarding loop and our node.
click dronecan-connect
expect config.dronecan.button Disconnect
expect config.dronecan.connected true
expect config.dronecan.lists.enabled false
expect config.dronecan.filter.enabled true
expect config.dronecan.bus MAVLinkCAN1
expect config.dronecan.node.running true
expect config.dronecan.forwards > 1
expect config.dronecan.run true
expect config.dronecan.frames.sent > 1
# Node 127, heard from itself: its row, then its words, then its name.
expect config.dronecan.nodes 1
expect config.dronecan.node.127.health OK
expect config.dronecan.node.127.mode OPERATIONAL
expect config.dronecan.node.127.name org.missionplanner
expect config.dronecan.node.127.swversion ~ 0.1.

# The row, and its menu.
click dronecan-row-127
expect config.dronecan.current 127
click dronecan-row-127-menu
expect config.dronecan.menu true
click dronecan-menu-parameters
expect config.dronecan.menu false
expect config.dronecan.progress Getting Params
# Nobody answers param.GetSet for node 127: two seconds, then the window, empty.
expect config.dronecan.window params
expect config.dronecan.progress none
expect config.dronecan.params.node 127
expect config.dronecan.params.rows 0
click dronecan-params-close
expect config.dronecan.window none

# Restart: four requests a second apart, the answer not looked at.
click dronecan-row-127-menu
click dronecan-menu-restart
expect config.dronecan.restarts 1
expect config.dronecan.restarts 0

# Filter: every type, the page's ticked; ALL sends CAN_FILTER_MODIFY.
click dronecan-filter
expect config.dronecan.window filter
expect config.dronecan.filter.boxes 155
expect config.dronecan.filter.sent 0
click dronecan-filter-all
expect config.dronecan.filter.sent 1
click dronecan-filter-close
expect config.dronecan.window none

# Stats.
click dronecan-stats
expect config.dronecan.window stats
click dronecan-stats-close
expect config.dronecan.window none

# Inspector is not ported: the status line says so, and nothing opens.
click dronecan-inspector
expect config.dronecan.window none

# Disconnect: the bus stopped, the lists back.
click dronecan-connect
expect config.dronecan.button Connect
expect config.dronecan.connected false
expect config.dronecan.bus none
expect config.dronecan.lists.enabled true
expect config.dronecan.node.running false
# The rows stay until the next Connect empties them.
expect config.dronecan.nodes 1

# Connect again and leave the page: Deactivate is Disconnect.
click dronecan-connect
expect config.dronecan.bus MAVLinkCAN1
click setup-page-ConfigOptional
expect config.dronecan.active false
expect config.dronecan.bus none
expect config.dronecan.button Connect
